{"id":279,"date":"2020-11-18T18:23:10","date_gmt":"2020-11-18T23:23:10","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.fm1.dev\/hearing-aid\/redux\/"},"modified":"2024-01-05T19:04:23","modified_gmt":"2024-01-06T00:04:23","slug":"redux","status":"publish","type":"page","link":"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/hearing-aids\/redux\/","title":{"rendered":"Redux Hearing Aid Restoration"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p>Want to make sure that you get as many uses as possible, regardless of whatever <a href=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/hearing-aids\/\" data-type=\"URL\" data-id=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/hearing-aids\/\">type of hearing aid<\/a> you wear? It\u2019s important to bring your hearing technology in regularly for maintenance and cleaning, though there\u2019s another potential hindrance that might result from repeated use or exposure to the elements: moisture.<\/p>\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-image\">\n<figure class=\"alignright size-full is-resized\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/redux.png\" alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-31548\" width=\"460\" height=\"258\" srcset=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/redux.png 1200w, https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/redux-768x432.png 768w, https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2024\/01\/redux-600x338.png 600w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 460px) 100vw, 460px\" \/><\/figure>\n<\/div>\n\n\n<p>That\u2019s why Elevate Audiology offers <a rel=\"noreferrer noopener\" href=\"https:\/\/redux.com\/the-science-tech-behind-redux-products\/\" target=\"_blank\">Redux commercial-grade drying services<\/a>, which ensures that you get the most out of your hearing aids, regardless of any unfortunate encounters with water.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What\u2019s the Problem?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Like most electronic devices, excess moisture can stop hearing aids from working properly over time. Exposure to rain, snow and other elements may also cause irreparable damage to your new devices.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>This is especially problematic since at least 98% of all hearing aids have some form of moisture in them at any given moment, in addition to more than 60% of out-of-warranty hearing aid repairs being related to water damage.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Once the damage is done, your hearing aids may not turn on or sounds you\u2019ve regrown accustomed to may now become faint or distorted.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\">What Can You Do?<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p>Thankfully, you have options. Redux works to remove air pressure from your hearing aid\u2019s chamber through a tested and tried vacuum system, which allows any remaining moisture to evaporate during the procedure.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Redux is a safe, effective and scientifically proven solution to keep your hearing aids up and running for the long haul. It\u2019s used nationwide to help restore many hearing aids and, in some cases, even cell phone and tablet technology.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Want to learn more about Redux hearing aid drying or have questions about the process? <a href=\"https:\/\/elevateaudiology.com\/x-about-us\/location\/\" data-type=\"page\" data-id=\"115\">Contact us<\/a> to schedule an appointment with the experts at Elevate Audiology today.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p>Call Elevate Audiology at <a href=\"tel:(864) 447-6611\">(864) 447-6611<\/a> for the Easley office or <a href=\"tel:(864) 447-4183\">(864) 447-4183<\/a> for the Greenville office for more information or to schedule an appointment.<\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Want to make sure that you get as many uses as possible, regardless of whatever type of hearing aid you wear? It\u2019s important to bring your hearing technology in regularly for maintenance and cleaning, though there\u2019s another potential hindrance that might result from repeated use or exposure to the elements: moisture. That\u2019s why Elevate Audiology&#8230;<\/p>\n","protect